{
  "manufacturer": "CoolAutomation",
  "manufacturer_slug": "coolautomation",
  "model": "CoolMasterNet Mitsubishi Electric PUHV-P CM-E outdoor unit (PRO) objects",
  "model_slug": "coolmasternet-mitsubishi-puhv-p-cm-e-outdoor",
  "aliases": [
    "Mitsubishi City Multi BACnet",
    "CoolMasterNet Mitsubishi Electric",
    "PUHV-P CM-E"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "VRF outdoor unit monitoring via BACnet gateway",
  "applies_to": "Mitsubishi Electric PUHV-P [capacity] CM-E outdoor units (the guide heading ends in \"CM-E/...\" without naming the other suffixes) read through a CoolAutomation gateway with PRO functionality.",
  "summary": "With PRO functionality, CoolAutomation gateways publish service data from Mitsubishi Electric City Multi PUHV-P CM-E outdoor units over BACnet: type, control and operation mode, compressor and fan frequencies, total cooling and heating capacity, LEV positions, compressor currents and bus voltage, 63HS/63LS pressures, thermistor, condensing and evaporating temperatures, operation status and OC/OS attribute, plus subcooling and superheat values and box temperature (54 objects). Monitoring only.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP",
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": 64,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Instance = VA x 256 + index (object identifier bits 21-8 = VA, 7-0 = index). Points shown for VA 1; the guide does not explain how outdoor units receive their VA.",
    "Access set to read-only: these are measured service values, although the guide's type table lists PIV as read/write.",
    "Object names are the guide's short names; descriptions are the guide's object descriptions with the bracketed unit moved to units.",
    "Table printed on page 271 of the guide (section 3.2.6.2).",
    "Coded values (operation mode, control mode, operation status and similar) are explained in the guide's ME PRO Enumerated Parameters tables and are not repeated here.",
    "The guide also prints Mitsubishi Electric tables under generic headings such as 'PURY-P [capacity]' or 'PUHY-P [capacity]'; read the Type object (CSV 256) and compare a discovery with this list before mapping.",
    "The guide lists no error-code object in this table.",
    "The guide prints separate tables for PUHV-P SCM-E units; they are not covered here."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "BACnet Integration Guidelines - CoolMaster Product Line, CooLinkNet, CooLinkHub, CooLinkBridge",
    "doc_number": null,
    "revision_date": "Rev 1.0.4, 2026-07-06",
    "url": "https://support.coolautomation.com/hc/en-us/article_attachments/38262832368157"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Use these objects to monitor Mitsubishi Electric equipment only; control stays on the CoolMasterNet indoor-unit objects. Map the block's VA and trend operation mode, compressor frequency and pressures.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "PIV 258",
        "name": "OpeM",
        "why": "Operation mode code"
      },
      {
        "ref": "PIV 280",
        "name": "OpeS",
        "why": "Operation status code"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 306",
        "name": "CompOn",
        "why": "Compressor on"
      },
      {
        "ref": "PIV 260",
        "name": "F1",
        "why": "Compressor 1 frequency, Hz"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 271",
        "name": "63HS1",
        "why": "High pressure, kg/cm2"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 272",
        "name": "63LS",
        "why": "Low pressure, kg/cm2"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 287",
        "name": "Tc",
        "why": "Condensing temperature, °C"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 288",
        "name": "Te",
        "why": "Evaporating temperature, °C"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "BACnet must be enabled on the gateway; these objects belong to its PRO (service data) functionality.",
    "heartbeat": null,
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "BACnet MS/TP: activate on line L3 with 'line type L3 BAC' (L4-L7 also possible on the CoolMaster product line); default frame 9600 8N1, change with 'line baud L3 <rate>_8N1'; MAC (TS) default 0x40 = 64, change with 'line myid L3 <hex>'. Reboot after each change.",
      "BACnet IP: enable with 'bacnet IP enable'; UDP port 47808 by default ('bacnet port <n>'). The server starts only once Ethernet is up with an IP address.",
      "Default device instance 64 (0x40); change with 'bacnet instance <n>'."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "The guide does not document how VAs are assigned to outdoor units; confirm instances with a BACnet discovery."
    ]
  },
  "covers_brands": [
    "Mitsubishi Electric"
  ],
